  "term": "reciprocal inhibition",
  "definition": "Reciprocal inhibition is the suppression of motoneuron activity by Ia inhibitory interneurons that arise from the embryonic V1 progenitor domain. In this packet, it is described as a spinal cord inhibitory process involving motoneurons.",
